# Build context is backend/, so every path here is relative to backend/.
#
# This file is the primary control on what can *possibly* end up in a layer.
# Layers are immutable: a file COPYed in and deleted by a later instruction is
# still present in the earlier layer and readable by anyone who pulls the image.
# Excluding it here means it never enters the build context at all, so no
# instruction can copy it even by accident.

# ─── Secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The whole point. .env holds SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY, which bypasses RLS, and
# SUPABASE_DB_URL, which carries the database password. Neither may reach a
# layer. The glob also covers .env.local / .env.production, and .env.example
# too -- documentation the running container has no use for.
# Both anchored and any-depth forms, since docker does not imply the second.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# ─── Test-only material ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not needed at runtime. tests/conftest.py reads SUPABASE_DB_URL and
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY and documents the shape of the test credentials, and
# requirements-dev.txt would drag pytest and psycopg into the image for nothing.
tests/
**/tests/
pytest.ini
requirements-dev.txt

# ─── Local virtualenv ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hundreds of MB, built against the host's Python, and would shadow or conflict
# with the packages pip installs inside the image. Never useful in a container.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ─── Python caches ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Host-generated bytecode is invalid in the image anyway, and copying it in
# would defeat PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE.
#
# The **/ prefix is load-bearing. Docker's ignore patterns are NOT gitignore's:
# a bare `__pycache__/` anchors to the context root and matches only a top-level
# directory, so models/__pycache__ and services/__pycache__ were copied in until
# this was corrected. gitignore treats the same pattern as "at any depth"; docker
# needs **/ said explicitly.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# ─── Documentation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENV_VARS.md is an inventory of every variable and which are secret. Useful to
# you, pure reconnaissance to anyone who pulls the image.
*.md

# ─── Build machinery itself ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# ─── Editor / OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Note: the repo's .git directory is at the repository root, one level above
# this build context, so the git history is already outside the build entirely.
# That is a deliberate reason to build from backend/ rather than the repo root.
